On Feb 7,  7:00pm, J"org Knappen wrote:

> MakeIndex 2.11 is publically available, I fetched it only a few weeks ago
> from niord.shsu.edu for the VAXen here. Version 3.* I have never seen in
> the public area.

Yes, I know, but so is 2.09, and my point was that there is a lack
of clarity on the fact that 2.11 is an upgrade which should totally
supersede 2.09 on all platforms, as TeX 3 should blot out TeX 2.  I
fear that a) many ordinary users are not aware that they can and should
upgrade, b) because up to now there has been no "managerial control"
of Makeindex (the original authors have apparently been unreachable
for some years), nobody has made concrete announcements on the matter.
Recurrent messages in the TeX fora show that many people are still using
2.09.

I also know that 3.0.8 is not publicly available, and in spite of
Joachim's hesitations about the quality of the code, I strongly
believe that 3.0.8 (or later, of course) deserves to be distributed.
This has to come from Joachim, of course.  I am hoping that this
discussion will reach him, and he may be moved to release 3.0.8,
or to discuss his aims with David Love.
Dominik


